  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 128 PM MST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nFriday...A slow moving shortwave trough aloft sweeps from western \nWyoming in the morning, to eastern Wyoming by evening, spawning a \nslight chance of showers for our Snowy and Sierra Madre Ranges and \nsouthern Laramie Valley, with dry conditions elsewhere. Cooler \ntemperatures for most locations due to an increase in cloud cover \nand a passing weak cold front.\n\nSaturday...Will see a slow warming trend though tempered by \nnortherly flow aloft. Low and mid levels look too dry for any \nprecipitation.\n\nSunday...The warming trend continues as the ridge aloft builds \nacross our counties, helping to produce a surface lee trough across \neastern Wyoming. 700 mb temperatures near 7 Celsius will yield \nmaximum temperatures from the mid 50s to mid 60s.\n\nMonday-Wednesday...Dry west northwest flow aloft prevails with a few \nshortwave troughs aloft passing by, though with minimal low and mid \nlevel moisture, no precipitation expected. High temperatures nearly \nthe same each day based on 700 mb temperatures.",
